e pawn structure prematurely.\n\nReason:  \nN:g8-f6 is a highly principled developing move that activates a piece, prepares for castling, and exerts influence over the center. It avoids premature pawn commitments while following opening principles. It’s one of the most common and effective first moves in many openings (e.g., the Alekhine Defense or after 1.e4 e5).\n\nAnswer: N: g8-f6'}
